# Mobile Responsiveness (mandatory)

Every UI change — client, admin, marketing, auth, modals — must work on ~375px and up. **Page-level horizontal scrolling is forbidden.**

## Hard rules
- Layout must fit the viewport width; only **vertical** page scroll
- Contained horizontal scroll is OK only inside tables/carousels (`.table-scroll`, overflow-x-auto on a bounded child) — never on `html`/`body`/`#root`
- Flex/grid children that can grow: always `min-w-0` (and often `max-w-full`) on the scroll column
- Prefer responsive stacks: `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2`, wrap toolbars with `flex-wrap gap-*`
- Wide tables: wrap in `.table-scroll` + provide `DataGrid` `mobileCard` for `< sm`
- Admin chrome: desktop sidebar at `lg+`; below `lg` use the drawer/top bar — never a permanent wide sidebar on phones
- Long text/URLs/HTML: `break-words` / `break-all` on links; rich content gets `overflow-x-auto` + `min-w-0`
- No fixed widths wider than the viewport without `max-w-full` / `min(..., 100%)`
- Avoid negative horizontal margins (`-mx-*`) that escape padded cards on small screens

## Validate before finishing
1. Mentally (or in browser) check **375px** and **768px**
2. Confirm no document `overflow-x` / sideways drag
3. Tap targets usable; primary actions not clipped off-screen

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — forces page-wide scroll
<div className="flex">
  <aside className="w-[272px] shrink-0" />
  <main className="flex-1">{/* wide table */}</main>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="flex max-w-[100vw] overflow-hidden">
  <aside className="hidden lg:flex w-[272px] shrink-0" />
  <main className="min-w-0 max-w-full flex-1 overflow-x-hidden">{children}</main>
</div>
```
